                                                "example_id": "1a4c521f-c0f5-4472-9765-4ddf23ec9972",
                                                "sense_id": "230ada69-8292-3f98-9e17-ecc11da425e5",
                                                "text": "You don’t have to be a member of a tribe to help protect native languages. In Oklahoma, public students can choose to take Indigenous language courses like Bodéwadmimwen, Cherokee, Chickasaw, Comanche and others for school credit — an empowering step toward recognition and respect. Many tribal nations, including CPN, also offer free resources such as language apps, workshops and virtual lessons open to learners of all backgrounds and abilities."
